1793 - Execution of Marie Antoinette 1834 - Fire swept through the Palace of Westminster 1859 - Raid on the Harpers Ferry arsenal, Virginia by John Brown 1902 - First Borstal institution opened (in Borstal, Kent) 1964 - China exploded her first nuclear bomb 1964 - Return of the first Labour Government for 13 years at the general election 1978 - Karol Wojtyla, Archbishop of Krakow, elected Pope
